<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-F008>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-F008" ;
  triage:title "Wire answers carry invariants as raw primitives. JevAnswer::Noul { probabilities: BTreeMap" ;
  triage:description "Wire answers carry invariants as raw primitives. JevAnswer::Noul { probabilities: BTreeMap<String, f64> } must be 'exactly {yes: p}'. confidence and probabilities are bare f64 in [0,1], checked only in into_answers. CheckResponse::model is String while CheckRequest::model is ModelId. A stray 'confidence' on a noul answer is accepted because deny_unknown_fields is absent. Recommendation: Use a NoulProbabilities { yes } struct with deny_unknown_fields. Use a validated Probability newtype for new jev::v1 and llm::v1 fields where this does not change moved types. Type the response model as ModelId." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBP" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
